  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Accenture Federal Services has $338M in contract obligations in FY2027 to date, across 70 awards with an average award size of $4.8M. Obligations are down 90.7% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer in FY2027 to date with $151M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services with $69.5M and the Department of Energy with $28.4M. Computer Systems Design Services is the dominant market with $326M in obligations, while Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services accounts for $10.5M. Historical context shows prior fiscal years with materially larger totals: FY22 totaled $3B, FY23 totaled $3.2B, FY24 totaled $3.7B, FY25 totaled $3.5B, and FY26 totaled $3.6B. Current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date activity. The figures below summarize buying-agency concentration and market mix so contractors and program managers can quickly see where Accenture Federal Services is working this fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Where are Accenture Federal Services' obligations coming from?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buyer with $151M. The Department of Health and Human Services follows with $69.5M and the Department of Energy with $28.4M. Accenture Federal Services also has obligations from the General Services Administration at $28M and several other agencies including Department of Homeland Security at $14.6M and Department of Commerce at $12.6M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "Accenture Federal Services has $338M in obligations in FY2027 to date compared with $3B in FY22, $3.2B in FY23, $3.7B in FY24, $3.5B in FY25, and $3.6B in FY26. Obligations are down 90.7% year over year. The current-year total is partial and presented fiscal year to date."
      }
    ]
  },
